.TH VERIFY 2
.SH NAME
verify: laplacianorder, laplacian7order \- convergence-order verification for the Laplacians
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "verify.m";
verify := load Verify Verify->PATH;

(levels, err) := verify->laplacianorder(8, 5);
(levels, err) = verify->laplacian7order(8, 4);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Verify
checks that a discretization actually converges at the order it
claims to \(em verification (are we solving the equations right?) in
the numerical-methods sense, not validation (are they the right
equations?), and not just eyeballing that an error got smaller.
.PP
.B Laplacianorder
applies
.IR pde (2)'s
discrete 5-point Laplacian to the known function
.RI sin(2π x )sin(2π y )
on a periodic unit square \(em periodic specifically to avoid any
boundary-treatment order contaminating the measurement, isolating pure
interior-stencil accuracy \(em at
.IR n0 ", 2" n0 ", 4" n0 ", ..."
resolution for
.I levels
levels, and reports, at each level, the max-norm error against the
exact Laplacian and the observed convergence order versus the previous
level (0.0 at the first level, which has none).  A correctly
implemented centred 5-point stencil is 2nd order: order should climb
toward
.I 2.0
as resolution increases, e.g.
.IR 0.000 ", " 1.930 ", " 1.982 ", " 1.996 ", " 1.999
for
.IR n0 =8
over 5 levels.
.PP
The Laplacian is applied via one deliberately small explicit
.B diffuse()
sub-step rather than a new
.IR pde (2)
export: for a step
.I h
small enough that
.B diffuse
takes it unsubdivided,
.RI ( u \fIsub\fRnew\fR - u \fIsub\fRold\fR)/ h
is exactly the discrete Laplacian by construction of the explicit-Euler
update
.B diffuse
performs internally \(em which also keeps this check free of any time-
discretization question, measuring only the spatial operator.
.PP
.B Laplacian7order
is the same study for
.IR math (2)'s
.BR lap7 ,
the three-dimensional seven-point stencil
.IR amr (2)
sweeps with.
It applies that stencil to
.if n \{\
sin(2*pi*x)*sin(2*pi*y)*sin(2*pi*z)
.\}
.if t \{\
.I "sin 2\(*px sin 2\(*py sin 2\(*pz"
.\}
on a padded cube whose halo is filled with the exact function, which is
what
.B lap7
expects and removes boundary treatment from the measurement entirely \(em
the same purpose periodicity serves in the two-dimensional study.
.PP
It exists for the usual reason and for one more.
.B Lap7
is otherwise checked only by comparing it against the Limbo loop it
replaced, and that loop had never itself been checked against an
analytic Laplacian: two implementations of one misunderstanding agree
with each other perfectly.
A convergence study cannot be satisfied that way.
Observed: 1.978, 1.994, 1.999.
.SH SOURCE
.B /module/verify.m
.br
.B /appl/lib/verify.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR pde (2),
.IR sh-verify (1)
